[{"source":"edge","severity":"note","category":"boundary","title":"Golden .t1 per-tick index field is unvalidated — the T1 gate compares hash order only, never the tick indices on the re-blessed lines","location":"harness/manifest.odin:69-75 (read_manifest default case), harness/manifest.odin:136-141 (check_manifest loop)","evidence":"case:\n\t\t// a per-tick hash line: \"<index> <hex>\"\n\t\tv, okv := strconv.parse_uint(fields[1], 16)\n\t\tif okv {\n\t\t\tappend(&m.hashes, u64(v))\n\t\t}\n...\n\t\tfor i in 0..<len(hashes) {\n\t\t\tif hashes[i] != m.hashes[i] {\n\t\t\t\tappend(fails, fmt.tprintf(\"T1: STATE DIVERGENCE at tick %d: %016x != golden %016x\",\n\t\t\t\t\ti+1, hashes[i], m.hashes[i]))","detail":"Every changed body line of qos_manual/qos_emphasis/qos_auto/sla/qos_contention.t1 carries an index field that no validator reads; a hand-mangled or off-by-one-renumbered golden (e.g. indices 2..301) passes check_manifest silently since only positional hash order is compared.","recommended_fix":"In read_manifest, validate the index field (must equal len(m.hashes)+1) or in check_manifest re-derive it; reject goldens whose tick indices are not exactly 1..N."}]
